# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-trustedpaths-real-registry-flaky — the real-registry TRUSTEDPATHS round trip failed once for one profile, not reproducible
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-trustedpaths-concurrent-registry-updates
#+DATE: 2026-11-15

* Symptom

One full =make test= on pfenny (French Windows, over ssh, clautolisp 2.4.14)
failed =trustedpaths-real-registry-round-trip-on-windows= for ONE of the two
AutoCAD profiles:

#+begin_example
Software\Autodesk\AutoCAD\R24.1\ACAD-5101:40C\Profiles\Epure\Variables holds
C:\Users\PPBN02261\AppData\Local\Temp\alfe-trust-test-é-448319\...
#+end_example

The write had reported success for both profiles (the token-length check
passed), and the =<<Profil sans nom>>= profile held the entry.

* Not reproduced

- The same test run alone ten times in a row on pfenny: 10/10 pass.
- A traced trust / read / untrust on both profiles: correct.
- The next full alfe suite on pfenny (2726 checks): 0 failures.
- No AutoCAD, accoreconsole or BricsCAD was running.

* Suspects

- =%run-powershell= is wrapped in =ignore-errors= and =%hkcu-read-value=
  returns NIL on no output, so a PowerShell launch that failed under load
  reads as "the entry is absent" -- indistinguishable, in the old message,
  from a real miss.
- A concurrent read-modify-write of the same profile by another process.

* Also seen

=<<Profil sans nom>>= still holds =C:\msys64\tmp\alfe-trust-test-é-956769\...=,
left by an earlier run that never reached its untrust (a test entry the stale
sweep does not recognise, since it is not an alfe-generated workdir name).

* Next

2.4.15 makes the assertion print the value read back. On the next
occurrence, that value says which suspect it is: NIL means the PowerShell
read failed (then make the read retry, or distinguish failure from absence);
a value without the entry means something rewrote the profile.

* Resolved (clautolisp / alfe 2.4.16)

** Cause: two processes of one account, one value

The GitLab runner on pfenny runs as =COMMUN\PPBN02261=, the account a
developer's ssh session uses, so CI jobs and a =make test= share one HKCU.
On 2026-11-15 the failing pfenny run was concurrent with CI job 18045935821
(=test:alfe:windows=, MR !542), which failed the same test at 17:33:19 CET
for the OTHER profile (=<<Profil sans nom>>=). Each run read TRUSTEDPATHS,
appended its entry, and wrote back what it had read plus that entry: the
later write erased the earlier run's entry -- each run lost its entry on a
different profile, a classic lost update. The same race explains the
leftover entry under =Also seen=: a stale value holding it written back
after its untrust.

Neither suspect above was the cause, but the first was a real defect too:
a failed read was taken for an absent value. Trust would then have
replaced the user's whole TRUSTEDPATHS with alfe's lone entry, and untrust
reported success, dropping the journal line, while the entry stayed.

** Fix

- =*registry-write-function*= is a compare-and-set
  (SUBKEY NAME EXPECTED DATA KIND) -> :OK / :CHANGED / NIL. =%hkcu-write-value=
  compares and writes inside one PowerShell script holding the named mutex
  =Global\alfe-trustedpaths= (an abandoned mutex is taken over; one not
  obtained in 30 s answers :CHANGED).
- =%update-registry-value= recomputes a change from the value found when the
  write answers :CHANGED, up to =*registry-update-attempts*= (8), then warns.
  Trust and untrust (and the stale sweep) go through it.
- =%hkcu-read-value= answers (VALUES NIL :ABSENT) for a missing value and NIL
  for a failed read; its script and the write's run with
  =$ErrorActionPreference='Stop'= inside try/catch, so an exception prints
  ERROR instead of falling through to the success marker.
- A failed write keeps its journal line (the write may have landed); an
  entry already present (:UNCHANGED) is not journalled, not being ours.

** Tests

- Mocked: an entry written concurrently between our read and our write
  survives trust and untrust; a value that changes on every attempt is given
  up (bounded); an unreadable value is never written and keeps the journal
  line.
- Real registry, any Windows host: four threads add, then remove, their own
  entries in one scratch value under =HKCU\Software\clautolisp-tests=. With
  the old unconditional write substituted it fails ("all four entries are
  there"); with the fix it passes on pfenny.
- The AutoCAD-profile round trip now names its workdir like an alfe workdir
  (=alfe-trust-test-é\alfe-trusttest-<pid>-<tag>=), so the next sweep removes
  the entry of a killed test, and checks that the profile's OTHER entries are
  restored, ignoring entries another concurrent run adds or removes.
